{
  "id": "minimax-h3-singularity-pack",
  "name": "Community — MiniMax H3 (Singularity)",
  "version": "1.0.1",
  "author": "WarmBloodAban (AIGC-Singularity)",
  "nsfw": false,
  "minComfyuiVersion": "v0.34.0",
  "description": "A community merge-and-finetune of MiniMax H3 ref2va by WarmBloodAban ('AIGC-Singularity'), trained on HDR footage with, per the author, three days of pruning and weight clean-up. What we could verify: sharper close-up faces and readable distant faces, at the cost of a darker, calmer image. Same official 20-step recipe and the same graphs as SimpliGen's own MiniMax H3 pack, one checkpoint for all three presets. MEASURED 2026-09-06 on a 12 GB RTX 4070 Ti, vanilla ComfyUI 0.34.3, against the official ref2va checkpoint with the same prompt, seed and settings (672x384, 5 s, 20 steps, three seeds each): reference-to-video close-ups are about 30% sharper (Laplacian 8.1 vs 6.2) with defined lips and skin texture where the official model goes soft and waxy; faces stay readable at medium-long range during a sword fight where the official model smears them. The trade: it renders about 20 points darker with slightly lower contrast, and with roughly a quarter to a third less motion per frame. A prompt asking for hard afternoon sun came back as a shaded courtyard three seeds out of three. Treat it as a look - sharper, calmer, darker - not a free upgrade; if you want the brighter, busier reading, use the official pack or DaSiWa. Same render time as the official checkpoint. LICENCE: the model card says Apache-2.0, but this is a derivative of MiniMax H3 weights, which places it under the MiniMax H3 Community License like every other H3 checkpoint - check that licence before shipping anything made with it. Base encoder and VAEs are the official Comfy-Org files shared with the other H3 packs, so the only new download is the 21 GB checkpoint.",
